 of our eyes  adventure is certainly out there in one  of pixar's most memorable films up when  carl frederickson comes face to face  with his childhood hero turned arch  nemesis the missing explorer charles  muns at first months is a welcoming  heroic presence until he discovers that  carl and his young friend russell have  befriended the elusive bird creature  he's been hunting  then muntz's kindness turns to menace  and carl's greatest inspiration quickly  turns into his greatest threat muntz's  dark and twisted obsession leads him  down a dangerous path with a legion of  talking dogs and it's also what  ultimately leads to his downfall a  classic villain in a classic performance  months is the perfect villainous foil  for this daring and emotional adventure  toy story pixar's feature-length debut  wants you to believe that sid an  extremely creative child who expresses  himself through highly imaginative  frankenstein-esque toy operations is  some kind of terrible evil person he  wears shirts with skulls on them and  rides a skateboard so clearly sid is a  monstrous young adult who's not to be  trusted  [Music]  let's go home and play  [Music]  sid has no idea the impact he's having  on these objects until they rise from  the ground to traumatize him he just  sees them as blueprints for his own  array of experimentation and even though  sid is positioned as woody and buzz's  worst nightmare there's still something  charming about his own unique version of  playtime  in ratatouille chef skinner is the  snobbish commercial head chef currently  running the lake cousteaus restaurant  and he stands as the only person in the  way of linguini taking over as the  rightful blood heir of gusto's legacy  with skinner's sights set on using the  gusto name to brand a collection of  frozen meals his love of food has turned  to well absolute trash and no long-lost  relative of gusto is going to get in the  way of that luckily for us a certain rat  chef is just a tad too cunning for  skinner to carry out his nefarious  anti-culinary schemes though skinner  still provides enough memorable menace  and conflict to leave a mark in this  stunning picture  in pixar's a bug's life a colony of ants  must face off against the oppressive  grasshoppers who've been abusing them  for years and no grasshopper is held in  more fearful esteem than the leader of  the pests himself hopper the demonic  insect with a huge distaste for ants and  a hunger for whatever food he can get  his hands on in the storybook world of a  bug's life hopper is the perfect  villainous foil needed to inspire the  ants to face him in the film's climactic  showstopper of a performance where our  heroes take hopper's only true weakness  his fear of birds and use it against him  even a few decades on this early creepy  crawly villain is still an absolute  standout  the best trick a pixar film can play is  hiding the villain in plain sight and  the captivating coco plays this trick  beautifully with the film's leading  musical talent ernesto de la cruz  brought to life by benjamin bratt de la  cruz is a musician who captures the  hearts and minds of both the living and  the dead and he's the primary  inspiration behind miguel's guitar  playing ambitions but it's only when our  protagonist unexpectedly journeys to the  land of the dead that he finds that de  la cruz's whole act has been built on a  web of lies in which ernesto killed his  songwriting partner and took credit for  his work miguel's hero turns right into  miguel's villain and de la cruz rises to  become one of pixar's best villains  anton ego begins ratatouille as the  skeletal food critic positioned as the  one to bring ultimate doom to chef  cousteau and his restaurant ego sends  fear and menace through the likes of  everyone who crosses his path including  chef gusto himself who dies in the wake  of one of his negative reviews but when  ego tastes the food cooked by the film's  rodent protagonist remy his attitude  changes leading to a glowing review for  gusto's restaurant and one of the most  elegant and beautiful odes to the art of  criticism ever seen in cinema history i  will be returning to gusto soon  hungry  for more  anyone can cook and as anton ego shows  anyone can turn their villainy into pure  heroism by a story's end  a nefarious early pixar villain stinky  pete pulls the brilliant trick of hiding  his true intentions from you until the  last possible moment then pulling the  rug out from under you in the most  chilling ingenious way possible in the  central conflict of toy story 2 stinky  pete represents the opposite of woody's  playful past he's a toy who's never been  played with and he'd rather keep it that  way after all he's been constantly  rejected by society so if he can't be  played with well no one can a complex  character plagued by his own  insecurities this prospector is easily  one of pixar's most memorable evil doers  perhaps it's fitting that for us the  best pixar villain is the one who turns  the act of villainy right on its head in  the incredibles syndrome was just a  mild-mannered superhero obsessive  rejected by his all-time idol mr  incredible that rejection hit him right  in his core leading him down a tech  obsessed path towards outright maniacal  villainy and turning him into the  red-headed hyper-villainous  super-killing syndrome that commands  both the incredibles and this very list  yeah i saved the best inventions for  myself  a perfect villain is usually the one who  thinks they're the real hero of the  story and that can certainly be said for  syndrome as classic a villain as they  come in the pixar universe or any other  cinematic universe for that matter  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite pixar movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

